                "text": "**Analyzing Input Structures**\n\nI've been analyzing the input grid, focusing on the distinct elements: four corner markers of color A and an inner shape of color B. In example 1, I've observed that color A is represented by the value 1, and color B by the value 2. Further study required!\n\n\n**Determining Output Dimensions**\n\nI'm now focused on deducing how to derive the output grid's dimensions. It's clear that the bounding box defined by the corner elements plays a crucial role. I'm noting that the inner shape's dimensions (height and width) determine the output's dimensions. Example 2's bounding box is rows 2..4, cols 2..5 (height 3, width 4) for a 3x4 output, and 3 has a 3x5 output. I'm mapping inputs to the output dimensions now.\n\n\n",
